{"abstract":"Denoising Diffusion Models (DDMs) have emerged as a strong competitor to Generative Adversarial Networks (GANs). However, despite their widespread use in image synthesis and editing applications, their latent space is still not as well understood. Recently, a semantic latent space for DDMs, coined ‘h-space’, was shown to facilitate semantic image editing in a way reminiscent of GANs. The h-space is comprised of the bottleneck activations in the DDM’s denoiser across all timesteps of the diffusion process. In this paper, we explore the properties of h-space and propose several novel methods for finding meaningful semantic directions within it. We start by studying unsupervised methods for revealing interpretable semantic directions in pretrained DDMs. Specifically, we show that interpretable directions emerge as the principal components in the latent space. Additionally, we provide a novel method for discovering image-specific semantic directions by spectral analysis of the Jacobian of the denoiser w.r.t. the latent code. Next, we extend the analysis by finding directions in a supervised fashion in unconditional DDMs. We demonstrate how such directions can be found by annotating generated samples with a domain-specific attribute classifier. We further show how to semantically disentangle the found directions by simple linear projection. Our approaches are applicable without requiring any architectural modifications, text-based guidance, CLIP-based optimization, or model fine-tuning.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Haas, René","Huberman-Spiegelglas, Inbar","Mulayoff, Rotem","Grasshof, Stella","Brandt, Sami Sebastian","Michaeli, Tomer"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-747266"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"country":["Israel"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Technion - Israel Institute of Technology"],"keyword":["Diffusion","Faces","Latent Space","disentanglement"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"discovering interpretable directions in the semantic latent space of diffusion models","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://brosdocs.net/fg2024/267.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-747266","identifier":[{"id":"85199476974","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-db60d9da-0207-4961-832b-587c2449946f"],"keyword":["diffusion","disentanglement","faces","latent space"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-33499E9963BD2CCB6EED9145511615F5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://brosdocs.net/fg2024/267.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"il","key":"technion israel institute of technology","loc":["Israel","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"name":"Technion - Israel Institute of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René","key":"haaspau","last":"Haas","name":"Haas, René","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Inbar","key":"hubermanspiegelglaspau","last":"Huberman-Spiegelglas","name":"Huberman-Spiegelglas, Inbar","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rotem","key":"mulayoffpau","last":"Mulayoff","name":"Mulayoff, Rotem","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stella","key":"graßhofpau","last":"Graßhof","locid":"ad50bed7-77fd-4c7f-819c-54455506e3f0","name":"Grasshof, Stella","name_org":"Graßhof, Stella","orcid":"0000-0002-6791-7425","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sami Sebastian","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"e8e88610-5144-41da-95bf-597abf1d7869","name":"Brandt, Sami Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-2141-9815","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Tomer","key":"michaelipau","last":"Michaeli","name":"Michaeli, Tomer","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"18th IEEE International Conference on Automatic Face and Gesture Recognition"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-db60d9da-0207-4961-832b-587c2449946f"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Discovering Interpretable Directions in the Semantic Latent Space of Diffusion Models","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-747266","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The contribution of forests to carbon storage and biodiversity conservation highlights the need for accurate forest height and biomass mapping and monitoring. In France, forests are managed mainly by private owners and divided into small stands, requiring 10 to 50 m spatial resolution data to be correctly separated. Further, 35 % of the French forest territory is covered by mountains and Mediterranean forests which are managed very extensively. In this work, we used a deep-learning model based on multi-stream remote-sensing measurements (NASA's Global Ecosystem Dynamics Investigation (GEDI) lidar mission and ESA's Copernicus Sentinel-1 and Sentinel-2 satellites) to create a 10 m resolution canopy height map of France for 2020 (FORMS-H). In a second step, with allometric equations fitted to the French National Forest Inventory (NFI) plot data, we created a 30 m resolution above-ground biomass density (AGBD) map (Mg ha-1) of France (FORMS-B). Extensive validation was conducted. First, independent datasets from airborne laser scanning (ALS) and NFI data from thousands of plots reveal a mean absolute error (MAE) of 2.94 m for FORMS-H, which outperforms existing canopy height models. Second, FORMS-B was validated using two independent forest inventory datasets from the Renecofor permanent forest plot network and from the GLORIE forest inventory with MAE of 59.6 and 19.6 Mg ha-1, respectively, providing greater performance than other AGBD products sampled over France. Finally, we compared FORMS-V (for volume) with wood volume estimations at the ecological region scale and obtained an R2 of 0.63 with an MAE of 30 m3 ha-1. These results highlight the importance of coupling remote-sensing technologies with recent advances in computer science to bring material insights to climate-efficient forest management policies. Additionally, our approach is based on open-Access data having global coverage and a high spatial and temporal resolution, making the maps reproducible and easily scalable. FORMS products can be accessed from 10.5281/zenodo.7840108 (Schwartz et al., 2023).","author_count":12,"contributors":["Schwartz, Martin","Ciais, Philippe","De Truchis, Aurélien","Chave, Jérôme","Ottlé, Catherine","Vega, Cedric","Wigneron, Jean-Pierre","Nicolas, Manuel","Jouaber, Sami","Liu, Siyu","Brandt, Martin","Fayad, Ibrahim"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-731878"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["France"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","INRAE","Institut national de l'information géographique et forestière","Kayrros SAS (Biz)","ONF, Office National des Forêts","Paris-Saclay University","Université Paul Sabatier Toulouse III"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"forms forest multiple source height wood volume and biomass maps in france at 000000000010 to 000000000030 m resolution based on sentinel 000000000001 sentinel 000000000002 and global ecosystem dynamics investigation gedi data with a deep learning approach","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5194/essd-15-4927-2023","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-731878","identifier":[{"id":"85178231845","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-98111361-86bb-4f26-a41a-1c40108d5d8b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CDBC6BD8A1BFEC174E95923AE2ADA158"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5194/essd-15-4927-2023","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/385695423/FORMS.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"fr","key":"paris saclay university","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Paris-Saclay University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fr","key":"kayrros sas","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Kayrros SAS (Biz)","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"fr","key":"université paul sabatier toulouse iii","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Université Paul Sabatier Toulouse III","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"fr","key":"institut national de l information géographique et forestière","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Institut national de l'information géographique et forestière","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"fr","key":"inrae","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"INRAE","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"fr","key":"onf office national des forêts","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"ONF, Office National des Forêts","used":1},{"affno":"7","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Geosciences and Natural Resource Management, Geography, Land, Environment and Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Martin","key":"schwartzpau","last":"Schwartz","name":"Schwartz, Martin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Philippe","key":"ciaispau","last":"Ciais","name":"Ciais, Philippe","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Aurélien","key":"detruchispau","last":"De Truchis","name":"De Truchis, Aurélien","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jérôme","key":"chavepau","last":"Chave","name":"Chave, Jérôme","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Catherine","key":"ottlépau","last":"Ottlé","name":"Ottlé, Catherine","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Cedric","key":"vegapau","last":"Vega","name":"Vega, Cedric","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Jean-Pierre","key":"wigneronpau","last":"Wigneron","name":"Wigneron, Jean-Pierre","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"Manuel","key":"nicolaspau","last":"Nicolas","name":"Nicolas, Manuel","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sami","key":"jouaberpau","last":"Jouaber","name":"Jouaber, Sami","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","first":"Siyu","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","locid":"0609c26a-3317-4f73-afe3-fc261c5fd28a","name":"Liu, Siyu","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","first":"Martin","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"ff0528eb-4f80-444b-a7ad-2d2307f7bdc9","name":"Brandt, Martin","orcid":"0000-0001-9531-1239","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Ibrahim","key":"fayadpau","last":"Fayad","name":"Fayad, Ibrahim","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.5194/essd-15-4927-2023","issn":["18663508","18663516"],"issn_org":["18663508"],"issue":"11","journal":"Earth System Science Data","pages":"4927-4945","status":"p","title":"Earth System Science Data","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85178231845"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-98111361-86bb-4f26-a41a-1c40108d5d8b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"FORMS : Forest Multiple Source height, wood volume, and biomass maps in France at 10 to 30 m resolution based on Sentinel-1, Sentinel-2, and Global Ecosystem Dynamics Investigation (GEDI) data with a deep learning approach","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-731878","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Though continuous advances in the field of human pose estimation, it remains a challenge to retrieve high-quality recordings from real-life human motion using commodity hardware. Therefore, this work focuses on predicting and improving estimates for human motion with the aim of achieving production quality for skinned mesh animations by off-the-shelf webcams. We take advantage of recent findings in the field by employing a recurrent neural network architecture to (1) predict and (2) denoise human motion, with the intention of bridging the gap between cheap recording methods and high-quality recording. First, we propose an LSTM to predict short-term human motion, which achieves competitive results to state-of-the-art methods. Then, we adapt this model architecture and train it to clean up noisy human motion from two 3D low-quality input sources, and hence mimic a real-world scenario of recording human motion which yields noisy estimates. Experiments on simulated data show that the model is capable of significantly reducing noise, and it opens the way for future work to test the model on annotated data.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Grasshof, Stella","Bastholm, Mathias","Brandt, Sami Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-695298"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Animation denoising","Computer vision","Reconstruction","Recurrent neural networks"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"neural network based human motion predictor and smoother","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s42979-023-02195-0","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-695298","identifier":[{"id":"85173924871","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-d3ce6ed3-057d-474c-8d1a-7247c7ef1ed4"],"keyword":["Animation denoising","Computer vision","Recurrent neural networks","reconstruction"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-4000F32E69B6230BEDAB97442F15761C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/s42979-023-02195-0.pdf?pdf=button","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s42979-023-02195-0","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Marionette ApS"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stella","key":"grasshofpau","last":"Grasshof","locid":"ad50bed7-77fd-4c7f-819c-54455506e3f0","name":"Grasshof, Stella","orcid":"0000-0002-6791-7425","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mathias","key":"bastholmpau","last":"Bastholm","name":"Bastholm, Mathias","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sami Sebastian","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"e8e88610-5144-41da-95bf-597abf1d7869","name":"Brandt, Sami Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-2141-9815","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","marionette aps"]},"sid":["itu-d3ce6ed3-057d-474c-8d1a-7247c7ef1ed4"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Neural Network-Based Human Motion Predictor and Smoother","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-695298","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"In this paper, we present an approach for combining non-rigid structure-from-motion (NRSfM) with deep generative models, and propose an efficient framework for discovering trajectories in the latent space of 2D GANs corresponding to changes in 3D geometry. Our approach uses recent advances in NRSfM and enables editing of the camera and non-rigid shape information associated with the latent codes without needing to retrain the generator. This formulation provides an implicit dense 3D reconstruction as it enables the image synthesis of novel shapes from arbitrary view angles and non-rigid structure. The method is built upon a sparse backbone, where a neural regressor is first trained to regress parameters describing the cameras and sparse non-rigid structure directly from the latent codes. The latent trajectories associated with changes in the camera and structure parameters are then identified by estimating the local inverse of the regressor in the neighborhood of a given latent code. The experiments show that our approach provides a versatile, systematic way to model, analyze, and edit the geometry and non-rigid structures of faces.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Haas, René","Grasshof, Stella","Brandt, Sami Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-712543"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["3D Geometry Editing","Deep generative models","Latent Space Trajectories","Non rigid Structure from Motion","Sparse Neural Regressor"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"controllable gan synthesis using non rigid structure from motion","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2211.07195","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-712543","ids":["itu-9c146d5b-4be2-4a1c-9750-7232f5f4a1c6"],"keyword":["3D Geometry Editing","Deep Generative Models","Latent Space Trajectories","Non-rigid Structure-from-Motion","Sparse Neural Regressor"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-F11281333CB29EECE5397E58A1D6C8F6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2023W/GCV/html/Haas_Controllable_GAN_Synthesis_Using_Non-Rigid_Structure-From-Motion_CVPRW_2023_paper.html","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2211.07195","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René","key":"haaspau","last":"Haas","name":"Haas, René","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stella","key":"grasshofpau","last":"Grasshof","locid":"ad50bed7-77fd-4c7f-819c-54455506e3f0","name":"Grasshof, Stella","orcid":"0000-0002-6791-7425","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sami Sebastian","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"e8e88610-5144-41da-95bf-597abf1d7869","name":"Brandt, Sami Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-2141-9815","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"]},"sid":["itu-9c146d5b-4be2-4a1c-9750-7232f5f4a1c6"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Controllable GAN Synthesis Using Non-Rigid Structure-From-Motion","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-712543","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"In this paper, we use a tensor model based on the Higher-Order Singular Value Decomposition (HOSVD) to discover semantic directions in Generative Adversarial Networks. This is achieved by first embedding a structured facial expression database into the latent space using the e4e encoder. Specifically, we discover directions in latent space corresponding to the six prototypical emotions: anger, disgust, fear, happiness, sadness, and surprise, as well as a direction for yaw rotation. These latent space directions are employed to change the expression or yaw rotation of real face images. We compare our found directions to similar directions found by two other methods. The results show that the visual quality of the resultant edits are on par with State-of-the-Art. It can also be concluded that the tensor-based model is well suited for emotion and yaw editing, i.e., that the emotion or yaw rotation of a novel face image can be robustly changed without a significant effect on identity or other attributes in the images.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Haas, René","Grasshof, Stella","Brandt, Sami Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384783"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition","Face Synthesis","Generative adversarial network"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tensor based emotion editing in the stylegan latent space","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.06102","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384783","ids":["itu-eea42dca-6570-4bfe-ae45-18a9b15afdca"],"keyword":["Computer vision and pattern recognition","Face Synthesis","generative adversarial network"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-F995BED9613C9FCA062262739F0DEBA6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.06102","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René","key":"haaspau","last":"Haas","name":"Haas, René","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stella","key":"grasshofpau","last":"Grasshof","locid":"ad50bed7-77fd-4c7f-819c-54455506e3f0","name":"Grasshof, Stella","orcid":"0000-0002-6791-7425","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sami Sebastian","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"e8e88610-5144-41da-95bf-597abf1d7869","name":"Brandt, Sami Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-2141-9815","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-eea42dca-6570-4bfe-ae45-18a9b15afdca"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Tensor-based Emotion Editing in the StyleGAN Latent Space","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384783","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Recording real life human motion as a skinned mesh animation with an acceptable quality is usually difficult. Even though recent advances in pose estimation have enabled motion capture from off-the-shelf webcams, the low quality makes it infeasible for use in production quality animation. This work proposes to use recent advances in the prediction of human motion through neural networks to augment low quality human motion, in an effort to bridge the gap between cheap recording methods and high quality recording. First, a model, competitive with prior work in short-term human motion prediction, is constructed. Then, the model is trained to clean up motion from two low quality input sources, mimicking a real world scenario of recording human motion through two webcams. Experiments on simulated data show that the model is capable of significantly reducing noise, and it opens the way for future work to test the model on annotated data.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Bastholm, Mathias","Grasshof, Stella","Brandt, Sami Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384236"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Animation","Denoising","Motion capture","Noise","Recurrent neural networks","body motion"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"neural network based human motion smoother","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86569437/ICPRAM2022.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384236","identifier":[{"id":"85173943994","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-ca7722df-15e0-463f-8bcf-2ef2ae689980"],"keyword":["animation","body motion","denoising","motion capture","noise","recurrent neural networks"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-262F115295E3E4409607B5CDA06F4CF7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86569437/ICPRAM2022.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mathias","key":"bastholmpau","last":"Bastholm","name":"Bastholm, Mathias","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stella","key":"grasshofpau","last":"Grasshof","locid":"ad50bed7-77fd-4c7f-819c-54455506e3f0","name":"Grasshof, Stella","orcid":"0000-0002-6791-7425","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sami Sebastian","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"e8e88610-5144-41da-95bf-597abf1d7869","name":"Brandt, Sami Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-2141-9815","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"SCITEPRESS Digital Library","status":"p","title":"International Conference on Pattern Recognition Applications and Methods (ICPRA) 2022"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ca7722df-15e0-463f-8bcf-2ef2ae689980"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Neural Network-Based Human Motion Smoother","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384236","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"In this work we present a method that combines tensor-based face modelling and analysis and non-rigid structure-from-motion (NRSFM). The core idea is to see that the conventional tensor formulation for the face structure and expression analysis can be utilised while the structure component can be directly analysed as the non-rigid structure-from-motion problem. To the NRSFM problem part we further present a novel prior-free approach that factorises the 2D input shapes into affine projection matrices, rank-one 3D affine basis shapes, and the basis shape coefficients. The linear combination of the basis shapes thus yields the recovered 3D shapes upto an affine transformation. In contrast to most works in literature, no calibration information of the cameras or structure prior is required. Experiments on challenging face datasets show that our method, with and without the metric upgrade, is accurate and fast when compared to the state-of-the-art and is well suitable for dense reconstruction and face editing.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Grasshof, Stella","Brandt, Sami Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382525"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Non rigid Structure from Motion","tensor model"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tensor based non rigid structure from motion","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86569442/WACV2022_TensorNRSfM.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382525","ids":["itu-53f9665d-f889-4f89-9598-964d2faf879b"],"keyword":["non-rigid structure-from-motion","tensor model"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E38BB4B244B6C888C02454BCDC0E2852"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86569442/WACV2022_TensorNRSfM.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stella","key":"grasshofpau","last":"Grasshof","locid":"ad50bed7-77fd-4c7f-819c-54455506e3f0","name":"Grasshof, Stella","orcid":"0000-0002-6791-7425","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sami Sebastian","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"e8e88610-5144-41da-95bf-597abf1d7869","name":"Brandt, Sami Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-2141-9815","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"IEEE Winter Conference on Applications of Computer Vision (WACV) 2022"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-53f9665d-f889-4f89-9598-964d2faf879b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Tensor-Based Non-Rigid Structure from Motion","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382525","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"In this paper, we propose tGAN a tensor-based method for modeling the latent space of generative models. The objective is to identify semantic directions in latent space. To this end, we propose to fit a multilinear tensor model on a structured facial expression database, which is initially embedded into latent space. We validate our approach on StyleGAN trained on FFHQ using BU-3DFE as a structured facial expression database. We show how the parameters of the multilinear tensor model can be approximated by Alternating Least Squares. Further, we introduce a stacked style-separated tensor model, defined as an ensemble of style-specific models to integrate our approach with the extended latent space of StyleGAN. We show that taking the individual styles of the extended latent space into account leads to higher model flexibility and lower reconstruction error. Finally, we do several experiments comparing our approach to former work on both GANs and multilinear models. Concretely, we analyze the expression subspace and find that the expression trajectories meet at an apathetic face that is consistent with earlier work. We also show that by changing the pose of a person, the generated image from our approach is closer to the ground truth than results from two competing approaches.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Haas, René","Grasshof, Stella","Brandt, Sami Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383429"],"event":{"acronym":"FG (alt: FGR)","title":"IEEE International Conference on Automatic Face and Gesture Recognition"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["StyleGAN","tensor model"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tensor based subspace factorization for stylegan","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86569470/FG2021.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-383429","ids":["itu-932f1dd9-d173-4714-a623-bbccc7b41226"],"keyword":["StyleGAN","tensor model"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-69F03E70765E3C16E62F13EA038D0D5E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/356026652_Tensor-based_Subspace_Factorization_for_StyleGAN","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86569470/FG2021.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René","key":"haaspau","last":"Haas","name":"Haas, René","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stella","key":"grasshofpau","last":"Grasshof","locid":"ad50bed7-77fd-4c7f-819c-54455506e3f0","name":"Grasshof, Stella","orcid":"0000-0002-6791-7425","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sami Sebastian","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"e8e88610-5144-41da-95bf-597abf1d7869","name":"Brandt, Sami Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-2141-9815","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"IEEE International Conference on Automatic Face and Gesture Recognition 2021"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-932f1dd9-d173-4714-a623-bbccc7b41226"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Tensor-based Subspace Factorization for StyleGAN","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383429","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Abstract: Over the past 10 years, Oosterhof and Todorov’s valence–dominance model has emerged as the most prominent account of how people evaluate faces on social dimensions. In this model, two dimensions (valence and dominance) underpin social judgements of faces. Because this model has primarily been developed and tested in Western regions, it is unclear whether these findings apply to other regions. We addressed this question by replicating Oosterhof and Todorov’s methodology across 11 world regions, 41 countries and 11,570 participants. When we used Oosterhof and Todorov’s original analysis strategy, the valence–dominance model generalized across regions. When we used an alternative methodology to allow for correlated dimensions, we observed much less generalization. Collectively, these results suggest that, while the valence–dominance model generalizes very well across regions when dimensions are forced to be orthogonal, regional differences are revealed when we use different extraction methods and correlate and rotate the dimension reduction solution. Protocol registration: The stage 1 protocol for this Registered Report was accepted in principle on 5 November 2018. The protocol, as accepted by the journal, can be found at https://doi.org/10.6084/m9.figshare.7611443.v1.","author_count":241,"contributors":["Jones, Benedict C.","DeBruine, Lisa M.","Flake, Jessica K.","Liuzza, Marco Tullio","Antfolk, Jan","Arinze, Nwadiogo C.","Ndukaihe, Izuchukwu L.G.","Bloxsom, Nicholas G.","Lewis, Savannah C.","Foroni, Francesco","Willis, Megan L.","Cubillas, Carmelo P.","Vadillo, Miguel A.","Turiegano, Enrique","Gilead, Michael","Simchon, Almog","Saribay, S. Adil","Owsley, Nicholas C.","Jang, Chaning","Mburu, Georgina","Calvillo, Dustin P.","Wlodarczyk, Anna","Qi, Yue","Ariyabuddhiphongs, Kris","Jarukasemthawee, Somboon","Manley, Harry","Suavansri, Panita","Taephant, Nattasuda","Stolier, Ryan M.","Evans, Thomas R.","Bonick, Judson","Lindemans, Jan W.","Ashworth, 