,"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85098789303"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-f637088d-dde4-404d-bbca-b9629c75ff1c","ku-03e0d8e2-0648-45bb-87d0-9d88ff09bf83"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"To which world regions does the valence–dominance model of social perception apply?","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.79-822771","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"In this work, we present a new versatile 3D multilinear statistical face model, based on a tensor factorisation of 3D face scans, that decomposes the shapes into person and expression subspaces. Investigation of the expression subspace reveals an inherent low-dimensional substructure, and further, a star-shaped structure. This is due to two novel findings. (1) Increasing the strength of one emotion approximately forms a linear trajectory in the subspace. (2) All these trajectories intersect at a single point - not at the neutral expression as assumed by almost all prior works - but at an apathetic expression. We utilise these structural findings by reparameterising the expression subspace by the fourth-order moment tensor centred at the point of apathy. We propose a 3D face reconstruction method from single or multiple 2D projections by assuming an uncalibrated projective camera model. The non-linearity caused by the perspective projection can be neatly included into the model. The proposed algorithm separates person and expression subspaces convincingly, and enables flexible, natural modelling of expressions for a wide variety of human faces. Applying the method on independent faces showed that morphing between different persons and expressions can be performed without strong deformations.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Grasshof, Stella","Ackermann, Hanno","Brandt, Sami Sebastian","Ostermann, Jorn"],"cuid":["S02-094.59-038333"],"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Leibniz University Hannover","Leibniz Universität Hannover","University of Hanover"],"keyword":["3D reconstruction","HOSVD","Statistical shape model","expression transfer","person transfer","tensor model"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"multilinear modelling of faces and expressions","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86353553/tpami_pure.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-094.59-038333","identifier":[{"id":"85114612751","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32305893","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["itu-7aabbc12-7aeb-4bc2-8472-de92e1b3d9cd","ku-049650b6-2e5d-4624-a656-b92e6360f964"],"keyword":["3D-reconstruction","HOSVD","Statistical shape model","expression transfer","person transfer","tensor model"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-AA5FC79F751578EE6CD0CF951C3F7A4A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86353553/tpami_pure.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"leibniz universität hannover","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Leibniz Universität Hannover","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"university of hanover","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Hanover","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"leibniz university hannover","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Leibniz University Hannover","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Stella","key":"grasshofpau","last":"Grasshof","locid":"ad50bed7-77fd-4c7f-819c-54455506e3f0","name":"Grasshof, Stella","orcid":"0000-0002-6791-7425","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanno","key":"ackermannpau","last":"Ackermann","name":"Ackermann, Hanno","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 1","first":"Sami Sebastian","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"16b4d290-9775-4705-8e06-382641f16444","name":"Brandt, Sami Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-2141-9815","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jörn","key":"ostermannpau","last":"Ostermann","name":"Ostermann, Jörn","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32305893"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/tpami.2020.2986496","issn":["01628828"],"issue":"10","journal":"IEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence","pages":"3540-3554","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"IEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence","title_org":"I E E E Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence","volume":"43"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85114612751"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-7aabbc12-7aeb-4bc2-8472-de92e1b3d9cd","ku-049650b6-2e5d-4624-a656-b92e6360f964"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Multilinear Modelling of Faces and Expressions","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-094.59-038333","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Indexing and retrieving music based on emotion is a powerful retrieval paradigm with many applications. Traditionally, studies in the field of music emotion recognition have focused on training and testing supervised machine learning models using a single music dataset. To be useful for today’s vast music libraries, however, such machine learning models must be widely applicable beyond the dataset for which they were created. In this work, we analyze to what extent models trained on one music dataset can predict emotion in another dataset constructed using a different methodology, by conducting cross-dataset experiments with three publicly available datasets. Our results suggest that training a prediction model on a homogeneous dataset with carefully collected emotion annotations yields a better foundation than prediction models learned on a larger, more varied dataset, with less reliable annotations.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Hult, Sabina","Kreiberg, Line Bay","Brandt, Sami Sebastian","Jónsson, Björn Thór"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383247"],"event":{"acronym":"ICMR","title":"ACM International Conference on Multimedia Retrieval"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cross dataset","Model transferability","Music emotion recognition"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"analysis of the effect of dataset construction methodology on transferability of music emotion recognition models","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85669536/ICMR2020_Hult_Kreiberg_ICMRSP16.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383247","identifier":[{"id":"85086897683","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-8711cf95-2862-45c8-8a36-27666544d955"],"keyword":["Cross-dataset","Model transferability","Music emotion recognition"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-49E451FF732E5103E230C6CC34D2C70A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85669536/ICMR2020_Hult_Kreiberg_ICMRSP16.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Audio-Visual Computing","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Sabina","key":"hultpau","last":"Hult","name":"Hult, Sabina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Bay","key":"kreibergpau","last":"Kreiberg","name":"Kreiberg, Line Bay","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sami Sebastian","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"e8e88610-5144-41da-95bf-597abf1d7869","name":"Brandt, Sami Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-2141-9815","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Björn Thór","key":"jónssonpau","last":"Jónsson","name":"Jónsson, Björn Thór","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Cathal","key":"gurrinpedh","last":"Gurrin","name":"Gurrin, Cathal","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Björn Þór","key":"jónssonpedh","last":"Jónsson","name":"Jónsson, Björn Þór","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Noriko","key":"kandopedh","last":"Kando","name":"Kando, Noriko","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Klaus","key":"schöffmannpedh","last":"Schöffmann","name":"Schöffmann, Klaus","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Yi-Ping Phoebe","key":"chenpedh","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Yi-Ping Phoebe","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Noel E.","key":"oconnorpedh","last":"O'Connor","name":"O'Connor, Noel E.","rank":10,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3372278.3390733","eisbn":["9781450370875"],"pages":"316-320","place":"Dublin, Ireland","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the ACM International Conference on Multimedia Retrieval (ICMR)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85086897683"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-8711cf95-2862-45c8-8a36-27666544d955"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Analysis of the Effect of Dataset Construction Methodology on Transferability of Music Emotion Recognition Models","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383247","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"We propose a general, prior-free approach for the uncalibrated non-rigid structure-from-motion problem for modelling and analysis of non-rigid objects such as human faces. We recover the non-rigid affine structure and motion from 2D point correspondences by assuming that (1) the non-rigid shapes are generated by a linear combination of rigid 3D basis shapes, (2) that the non-rigid shapes are affine in nature, i.e., they can be modelled as deviations from the mean, rigid shape, (3) and that the basis shapes are statistically independent. In contrast to the majority of existing works, no statistical prior is assumed for the structure and motion apart from the assumption the that underlying basis shapes are statistically independent. The independent 3D shape bases are recovered by independent subspace analysis (ISA). Likewise, in contrast to the most previous approaches, no calibration information is assumed for affine cameras; the reconstruction is solved up to a global affine ambiguity that makes our approach simple and efficient. In the experiments, we evaluated the method with several standard data sets including a real face expression data set of 7200 faces with 2D point correspondences and unknown 3D structure and motion for which we obtained promising results.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Brandt, Sami Sebastian","Ackermann, Hanno","Grasshof, Stella"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381372"],"event":{"acronym":"ICCV","title":"International Conference on Computer Vision"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Leibniz Universität Hannover"],"keyword":["3D Shape Reconstruction","Affine Structure Recovery","Independent Subspace Analysis","Statistical Independence","Uncalibrated Non Rigid Structure from Motion"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"uncalibrated non rigid factorisation by independent subspace analysis","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85683429/Brandt_Uncalibrated_Non_Rigid_Factorisation_by_Independent_Subspace_Analysis_ICCVW_2019_paper.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381372","identifier":[{"id":"85082448778","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-076bc7b5-64f8-475c-8b8e-97efd82c09e1"],"keyword":["3D Shape Reconstruction","Affine Structure Recovery","Independent Subspace Analysis","Statistical Independence","Uncalibrated Non-Rigid Structure-from-Motion"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-54CA640F0EB9AF76A7D0D2B6C0065D80"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85683429/Brandt_Uncalibrated_Non_Rigid_Factorisation_by_Independent_Subspace_Analysis_ICCVW_2019_paper.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://openaccess.thecvf.com/content_ICCVW_2019/papers/RSL-CV/Brandt_Uncalibrated_Non-Rigid_Factorisation_by_Independent_Subspace_Analysis_ICCVW_2019_paper.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Audio-Visual Computing","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"leibniz universität hannover","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Leibniz Universität Hannover","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sami Sebastian","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"e8e88610-5144-41da-95bf-597abf1d7869","name":"Brandt, Sami Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-2141-9815","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanno","key":"ackermannpau","last":"Ackermann","name":"Ackermann, Hanno","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Stella","key":"grasshofpau","last":"Grasshof","name":"Grasshof, Stella","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/iccvw.2019.00070","eisbn":["9781728150239"],"publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"2019 IEEE/CVF International Conference on Computer Vision Workshop (ICCVW)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85082448778"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-076bc7b5-64f8-475c-8b8e-97efd82c09e1"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Uncalibrated Non-Rigid Factorisation by Independent Subspace Analysis","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381372","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Fully convolutional neural networks (FCNs) have proven to be powerful tools for medical image segmentation. We apply an FCN based on the U-Net architecture for the challenging task of semantic segmentation of dental panoramic radiographs and discuss general tricks for improving segmentation performance. Among those are network ensembling, test-time augmentation, data symmetry exploitation and bootstrapping of low quality annotations. The performance of our approach was tested on a highly variable dataset of 1500 dental panoramic radiographs. A single network reached the Dice score of 0.934 where 1201 images were used for training, forming an ensemble increased the score to 0.936.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Koch, Thorbjorn Louring","Perslev, Mathias","Igel, Christian","Brandt, Sami Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-483396"],"event":{"acronym":"ISBI","end":"2019-04-11","place":"Venice, it","start":"2019-04-08","title":"16th IEEE International Symposium on Biomedical Imaging, ISBI 2019","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Deep learning","Dental radiography","Fully convolutional neural network","Segmentation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-3SHA","DI-PR-ALL"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-3SHA","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"accurate segmentation of dental panoramic radiographs with u nets","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85073091535&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-483396","identifier":[{"id":"85073091535","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-967fee89-8e1c-48c1-8130-6435c1aa0ce0"],"keyword":["Deep learning","Dental radiography","Fully convolutional neural network","Pantomogram","Segmentation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9E9826AD8A6F218781485728A009D785"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"3shape","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-3SHA","l3nn":"3Shape","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"3Shape","namevar":["3Shape Medical A/S (Biz)"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-3SHA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Thorbjorn Louring","key":"kochpau","last":"Koch","locid":"76fced73-f001-4bd7-8b3a-8ccb1669bbfc","name":"Koch, Thorbjorn Louring","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mathis","key":"perslevpau","last":"Perslev","locid":"6eb12a17-626a-43c8-bce9-20babb8b3681","name":"Perslev, Mathias","name_org":"Perslev, Mathis","orcid":"0000-0002-0358-4692","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"igelpau","last":"Igel","locid":"4ecc5e2e-7589-4f9b-9f79-d5dd99f56311","name":"Igel, Christian","orcid":"0000-0003-2868-0856","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sami Sebastian","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"16b4d290-9775-4705-8e06-382641f16444","name":"Brandt, Sami Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-2141-9815","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/isbi.2019.8759563","eisbn":["9781538636411"],"pages":"15-19","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"ISBI 2019 - 2019 IEEE International Symposium on Biomedical Imaging"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85073091535"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-967fee89-8e1c-48c1-8130-6435c1aa0ce0"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Accurate segmentation of dental panoramic radiographs with u-NETS","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-483396","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"In this paper, we show that the affine, non-rigid structure-from-motion problem can be solved by rank-one, thus degenerate, basis shapes. It is a natural reformulation of the classic low-rank method by Bregler et al., where it was assumed that the deformable 3D structure is generated by a linear combination of rigid basis shapes. The non-rigid shape will be decomposed into the mean shape and the degenerate shapes, constructed from the right singular vectors of the low-rank decomposition. The right singular vectors are affinely back-projected into the 3D space, and the affine back-projections will also be solved as part of the factorisation. By construction, a direct interpretation for the right singular vectors of the low-rank decomposition will also follow: they can be seen as principal components, hence, the first variant of our method is referred to as Rank-1-PCA. The second variant, referred to as Rank-1-ICA, additionally estimates the orthogonal transform which maps the deformation modes into as statistically independent modes as possible. It has the advantage of pinpointing statistically dependent subspaces related to, for instance, lip movements on human faces. Moreover, in contrast to prior works, no predefined dimensionality for the subspaces is imposed. The experiments on several datasets show that the method achieves better results than the state-of-the-art, it can be computed faster, and it provides an intuitive interpretation for the deformation modes.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Brandt, Sami Sebastian","Ackermann, Hanno"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383070"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Leibniz Universität Hannover"],"keyword":["Computer vision","Non rigid Structure from Motion"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"non rigid structure from motion by rank one basis shapes","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dw","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1904.13271","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383070","ids":["itu-7a88b957-a018-4461-aaee-fc2adf72bf77"],"keyword":["computer vision","non-rigid structure-from-motion"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-3FC481B6111496C71AA909C7528DAE60"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1904.13271","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Audio-Visual Computing","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"leibniz universität hannover","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Leibniz Universität Hannover","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sami Sebastian","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"e8e88610-5144-41da-95bf-597abf1d7869","name":"Brandt, Sami Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-2141-9815","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanno","key":"ackermannpau","last":"Ackermann","name":"Ackermann, Hanno","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"11","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-7a88b957-a018-4461-aaee-fc2adf72bf77"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Non-Rigid Structure-From-Motion by Rank-One Basis Shapes","type":"Working Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383070","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"We propose a general, prior-free approach for the uncalibrated non-rigid structure-from-motion problem for modelling and analysis of non-rigid objects such as human faces. The word general refers to an approach that recovers the non-rigid affine structure and motion from 2D point correspondences by assuming that (1) the non-rigid shapes are generated by a linear combination of rigid 3D basis shapes, (2) that the non-rigid shapes are affine in nature, i.e., they can be modelled as deviations from the mean, rigid shape, (3) and that the basis shapes are statistically independent. In contrast to the majority of existing works, no prior information is assumed for the structure and motion apart from the assumption the that underlying basis shapes are statistically independent. The independent 3D shape bases are recovered by independent subspace analysis (ISA). Likewise, in contrast to the most previous approaches, no calibration information is assumed for affine cameras; the reconstruction is solved up to a global affine ambiguity that makes our approach simple but efficient. In the experiments, we evaluated the method with several standard data sets including a real face expression data set of 7200 faces with 2D point correspondences and unknown 3D structure and motion for which we obtained promising results.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Brandt, Sami Sebastian","Ackermann, Hanno","Grasshof, Stella"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384987"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Leibniz Universität Hannover"],"keyword":["Computer vision","Non rigid Structure from Motion"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"uncalibrated non rigid factorisation by independent subspace analysis","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dw","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83658175/1811.09132v1.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384987","ids":["itu-fd26f88b-1c21-4e89-b8bf-b1f01c28dbe5"],"keyword":["computer vision","non-rigid structure-from-motion"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1D5737FBE3CF3333135CD2B9F49D7C8F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83658175/1811.09132v1.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Audio-Visual Computing","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"leibniz universität hannover","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Leibniz Universität Hannover","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sami Sebastian","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"e8e88610-5144-41da-95bf-597abf1d7869","name":"Brandt, Sami Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-2141-9815","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanno","key":"ackermannpau","last":"Ackermann","name":"Ackermann, Hanno","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Stella","key":"grasshofpau","last":"Grasshof","name":"Grasshof, Stella","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-fd26f88b-1c21-4e89-b8bf-b1f01c28dbe5"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Uncalibrated Non-Rigid Factorisation by Independent Subspace Analysis","type":"Working Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384987","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"We propose an integral geometric approach for computing dual distributions for the parameter distributions of multilinear models. The dual distributions can be computed from, for example, the parameter distributions of conics, multiple view tensors, homographies, or as simple entities as points, lines, and planes. The dual distributions have analytical forms that follow from the asymptotic normality property of the maximum likelihood estimator and an application of integral transforms, fundamentally the generalised Radon transforms, on the probability density of the parameters. The approach allows us, for instance, to look at the uncertainty distributions in feature distributions, which are essentially tied to the distribution of training data, and helps us to derive conditional distributions for interesting variables and characterise confidence intervals of the estimates.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Brandt, Sami Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383912"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Computer vision","Integral geometry","multiple view geometry"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"integral geometric dual distributions of multilinear models","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dw","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83658140/1812.00882v1.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383912","ids":["itu-b57bda9f-68ad-4e52-9fbb-85d380a3f612"],"keyword":["computer vision","integral geometry","multiple view geometry"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-D116A26637B9263459EF97BD24985D1D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83658140/1812.00882v1.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Audio-Visual Computing","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sami Sebastian","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"e8e88610-5144-41da-95bf-597abf1d7869","name":"Brandt, Sami Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-2141-9815","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b57bda9f-68ad-4e52-9fbb-85d380a3f612"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Integral Geometric Dual Distributions of Multilinear Models","type":"Working Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383912","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Jensen, Katrine Hommelhoff","Brandt, Sami Sebastian","Shigematsu, Hideki","Sigworth, Fred J."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-465167"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Kv1 2","Liposome","Potassium channel"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"statistical modeling and removal of lipid membrane projections for cryo em structure determination of reconstituted membrane proteins","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-465167","identifier":[{"id":"000371193600006","type":"wos"},{"id":"84958109785","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC4866491","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"26835990","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-77d55766-be23-42bf-b6d3-00183613df13"],"keyword":["Higher-order singular value decomposition","Kv1.2","Liposome","Potassium channel","Single-particle reconstruction","Statistical shape modeling"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CA17E603835CF46EB8EE57B91E9EAE57"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, The Image Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Katrine Hommelhoff","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"379a4286-880b-4b99-8477-03f060d742a5","name":"Jensen, Katrine Hommelhoff","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sami Sebastian","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"16b4d290-9775-4705-8e06-382641f16444","name":"Brandt, Sami Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-2141-9815","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hideki","key":"shigematsupau","last":"Shigematsu","name":"Shigematsu, Hideki","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Fred J.","key":"sigworthpau","last":"Sigworth","name":"Sigworth, Fred J.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26835990"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jsb.2016.01.012","issn":["10478477","10958657"],"issn_org":["10478477"],"issue":"1","journal":"Journal of Structural Biology","pages":"49-60","status":"p","title":"Journal of Structural Biology","volume":"194"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84958109785"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-77d55766-be23-42bf-b6d3-00183613df13"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Statistical modeling and removal of lipid membrane projections for cryo-EM structure determination of reconstituted membrane proteins","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-465167","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"In this paper, we address the problem of imaging membrane proteins for single-particle cryo-electron microscopy reconstruction of the isolated protein structure. More precisely, we propose a method for learning and removing the interfering vesicle signals from the micrograph, prior to reconstruction. In our approach, we estimate the subspace of the vesicle structures and project the micrographs onto the orthogonal complement of this subspace. We construct a 2D statistical model of the vesicle structure, based on higher order singular value decomposition (HOSVD), by considering the structural symmetries of the vesicles in the polar coordinate plane. We then propose to lift the HOSVD model to a novel hierarchical model by summarizing the multidimensional HOSVD coefficients by their principal components. Along with the model, a solid vesicle normalization scheme and model selection criterion are proposed to make a compact and general model. The results show that the vesicle structures are accurately separated from the background by the HOSVD model that is also able to adapt to the asymmetries of the vesicles. This is a promising result and suggests even wider applicability of the proposed approach in learning and removal of statistical structures.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Jensen, Katrine Hommelhoff","Sigworth, Fred","Brandt, Sami Sebastian"],"cuid":["S02-089.12-012734"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Yale University"],"keyword":["Algorithms","Image Processing Computer Assisted","Journal Article","Membrane Proteins","Microscopy Electron Transmission","Models Biological","Models Statistical","Signal Processing Computer Assisted"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-ALX"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-ALX","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"removal of vesicle structures from transmission electron microscope images","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/TIP.2015.2504901","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-089.12-012734","identifier":[{"id":"PMC4871786","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85009387528","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26642456","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-02084ed3-e1d9-4318-9dfd-16459173d898","ku-df4ba739-e6f9-4315-89a2-ee9fddba39e8"],"keyword":["Algorithms","Cytoplasmic Vesicles","Image Processing, Computer-Assisted","Journal Article","Membrane Proteins","Microscopy, Electron, Transmission","Models, Biological","Models, Statistical","Signal Processing, Computer-Assisted"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-612ED8EAB83651FCD361F37FFD80AF41"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/TIP.2015.2504901","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, The Image Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"alexandra institute","l2":"DI-GTS","l2n":"GTS Institutes","l3":"DI-GTS-ALX","l3nn":"Alexandra Institute","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Alexandra Institute","namevar":["Alexandra Instituttet A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-GTS-ALX","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"yale university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Yale University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","country":"dk","first":"Katrine Hommelhoff","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"379a4286-880b-4b99-8477-03f060d742a5","name":"Jensen, Katrine Hommelhoff","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Fred J.","key":"sigworthpau","last":"Sigworth","name":"Sigworth, Fred J.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sami Sebastian","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"16b4d290-9775-4705-8e06-382641f16444","name":"Brandt, Sami Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-2141-9815","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26642456"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/tip.2015.2504901","issn":["10577149","19410042"],"issn_org":["10577149"],"issue":"2","journal":"IEEE Transactions on Image Processing","pages":"540-552","publisher":"Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.","status":"p","title":"IEEE Transactions on Image Processing","title_org":"I E E E Transactions on Image Processing","volume":"25"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85009387528"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All GTS Institutes","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GTS-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","GTS Institutes","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-02084ed3-e1d9-4318-9dfd-16459173d898","ku-df4ba739-e6f9-4315-89a2-ee9fddba39e8"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Removal of Vesicle Structures from Transmission Electron Microscope Images","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-089.12-012734","year":2016,"yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"This paper considers a novel application of x-ray imaging of planks, for the purpose of detecting knots in high quality furniture wood. X-ray imaging allows the detection of knots invisible from the surface to conventional cameras. Our approach is based on texture analysis, or more specifically, discriminative dictionary learning. Experiments show that the knot detection and segmentation can be accurately performed by our approach. This is a promising result and can be directly applied in industrial processing of furniture wood.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Hansson, Nils Mattias","Enescu, Alexandru","Brandt, Sami Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-416626"],"event":{"acronym":"MVA","end":"2015-05-22","place":"Tokyo, jp","start":"2015-05-18","title":"14th IAPR International Conference on Machine Vision Applications","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"knot detection in x ray images of wood planks using dictionary learning","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-416626","identifier":[{"id":"84941199782","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-26c105ed-dc0e-4315-9519-ca8ef8c33799"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3A0C0D983498C31CA4F046AD5ECF71AD"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person